# Build context for deploy/api.Dockerfile and deploy/web.Dockerfile (context = repo root).
#
# This file is about two things, and the second one is not obvious: keeping the context small
# keeps `docker build` fast, and it keeps the *disk* under control on a machine that has run out
# of it before. node_modules alone is several hundred megabytes that the image builds re-create
# from the lockfile anyway.
#
# It is also a safety net: never let a local secret or a local database volume enter an image
# layer, where it would survive every later `rm` in the same Dockerfile.

# Version control and editors
.git
.gitignore
.vs
.vscode
.idea
.claude
.config
.github

# .NET build output — the image builds its own
**/bin
**/obj
artifacts
TestResults

# Node / Angular build output and caches
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.angular
**/npm-debug.log*

# Never bake a secret or a local data volume into a layer
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/appsettings.*.local.json
**/*.pfx
**/*.key
.data
postgres-data
minio-data

# Not part of any image
docs
design
archive
Pages
tools
tests
*.md
!web/teren-pwa/README.md
